    "prompt": "Suppose that \\(f(x + 3) = 3x^2 + 7x + 4\\) and \\(f(x) = ax^2 + bx + c.\\) What is \\(a + b + c?\\)"
  },
  "schemaVersion": "3.0",
  "solutions": [
    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "math:polynomial-coefficient-sums",
        "cnm_196"
      ],
      "explanation": "Evaluating \\(f(x)=ax^2+bx+c\\) at \\(x=1\\) makes every power of \\(x\\) equal to \\(1\\), so\n\\[\nf(1)=a+b+c.\n\\]\nTo obtain \\(f(1)\\) from the given formula for \\(f(x+3)\\), choose \\(x=-2\\), since \\(-2+3=1\\). Then\n\\[\nf(1)=3(-2)^2+7(-2)+4\n=12-14+4=2.\n\\]\nTherefore \\(a+b+c=2\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
      "id": "evaluate-coefficient-sum",
